Z||000000||vinnywolfe||07-01-2000||06:03 PM||||here's the deal.  i am restoring (just about done) an 87 gt.  when i drove it home last year after i bought it ( it was a wreck!) it seemed to have some balls to it. there was an exhaust leak (which i still cant find) and it desperately needed an alignment, but i was excited to get this project done because i thought the car would be fun to drive. <BR> i took it for a spin to have an alignment done yesterday ( the car has now been sitting for about 9 months) it drove pretty good at first.  it seemed to have good acceleration and shift fine.  then a few miles down the road, it bogged down. it had absolutely no power at all.  it took forever to reach 60.  I GOT PASSED BY AN ICE CREAM TRUCK !!! it stalls at red lights and stop signs, but will  start right back up.<BR>i scanned for codes (sice the check engine light would come on intermittently) and got one for MAP/MAF.<P>PLEASE HELP ME!!!!<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||8
Z||000001||86SE||07-01-2000||06:18 PM||||My guess is that the MAP sensor is toast.  Without the MAP sensor you loose most engine control (except on my Fiero......) so that would explain the slow acceleration.<P>First I would check the electrical connections at the MAP sensor and the vaccume hose that connects to the bottom of it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||hugh||07-01-2000||07:27 PM||||I don't know how sitting for a long time could do it,but it very well may be the catalytic converter.They can kill power like you won't believe.One more possibility.Could any thing have gotten into your tailpipe?  One way to check the map sensor is to have the engine running and tap the sensor lightly with a screwdriver handle,if the engine stumbles it's the sensor.<p>[This message has been edited by hugh (edited 07-01-2000).]||||reg||1
